// Shared lifting guidance admitted by the native coding controller.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormLift {
  field SrMeasure = "2026-10-01";
  field SrLocalDraft = "2026-10-02";
  field SrNativeVoice = "2026-10-03";
  field SrHostWalk = "2026-10-04";
  def fl-session-rent() = "SESSION RENT: The caller measures provider usage at session opening and closing with observe/rented-turn-meter-run.fk; Codex cumulative readings include input, cached input, output and total deltas. A Claude Code session is read whole by observe/session-rent-run.bml: its transcript and its subagents', one count per requestId (input, cache write, cache read, output), beside the local voice's drafts for that session, one row in receipts/session-rent-ledger.jsonl. Cached input is part of input; reasoning is part of output. Missing usage is unknown, never zero. Retain local generated/injected IDs, failed attempts and verified functions/lines changed beside those readings. Keep drafting, lifting, repair and verification in the owned native checkpoint. Use the local allowance for changed approaches and focused evidence. Prefer rented help as high-level guidance for a specific unresolved decision, carrying the retained failure instead of restarting the work. " + SrMeasure() + " measure and admit this guidance. " + SrLocalDraft() + " complete routine transformations locally. " + SrNativeVoice() + " carry supported tasks through local repair, verification and landing. " + SrHostWalk() + " target three consecutive supported jobs with zero rented-token growth from selection through landing. This is a measured target, not a capability claim. Coordinator identity, rented_mind and event-share percentages do not establish zero token use. Keep remote access available. The current plan lives in docs/form-native-coding.md#direction-toward-zero-rented-coding. ";
  def fl-guidance() = "FORM/BML LIFTING: Preserve public behavior, evaluation order, ownership and release; read callers and helper contracts first. Write explicit module imports outside section [form.bml]. Prefer [], xs[0], xs[-1] for last, xs[1:] for remainder, len(xs), value.str(), + for numbers/strings/lists, and == for exact value comparison. String lengths and slices count bytes. State String, Number or Value contracts when another comparison relationship is intended. Use lexical lambdas, lazy ?: and ??, match, half-open start .. end and input-last |> where they clarify intent. Reuse map, filter, foldl, any? and all?; named accessors explain tuple positions. Use only choice for alternatives, try work catch care for local recovery, and fail for an unavailable option. Zero, false and empty lists remain answers. Keep findings and owned effects in the same checkpoint; repeat/again/retry retain asynchronous context. Classes group APIs; templates describe parameters and members without implying instance accessors, interface checking or specialization. Use BMF cursors for source spans and native admission to verify contracts; retain original bytes until publication. Name domain literals once, remove superseded flows after callers agree, and inspect live frames and measured cost. Native tools edit supplied resident documents without model-selected shell, network or provider calls. Read the candidate and actual checks before claiming a lift. ";
 }
}
